  "p276.setup": "Set up organization",
  "p276.review": "Review organization",
  "p276.note": "Sends Agent J one instruction: organize the project folders you use with the workflow design method and register every CEO in the roster. Nothing is deleted or moved.",
  "p276.unreg": "Not in the CEO roster",
  "p276.starterTitle": "No workflows found yet. Agent J comes with three; install one to start:",
  "p276.starterTag": "Comes with Agent J · not installed",
  "p276.install": "Install it",
  "p276.s1name": "Knowledge base",
  "p276.s1desc": "Turns your notes and sources into a searchable, linked personal knowledge base.",
  "p276.s2name": "Scripts and articles",
  "p276.s2desc": "From topic to finished draft: video scripts and articles.",
  "p276.s3name": "E-book",
  "p276.s3desc": "Plans, writes and proofreads an e-book chapter by chapter.",
  "p276.installPrompt": "Please install the workflow `{id}` ({name}) that comes with Agent J from the Plaza: run `agentj plaza install {id}` and show me the preview first; install only after I agree. Then run `agentj wizard register --dir . --json` to put it in the CEO roster, and tell me when it shows on the phone's Workflows page.",
  "p276.setupPrompt": "Please use the agentj-workflow-wizard skill (the Workflow Design Bible method) to set up my organization:\n1. Look at the folders one level under the working root and find the projects I actually use;\n2. For those already organized this way (an entry file and the documentation/ boot documents), only review them; fill gaps with `agentj wizard apply`, never over files I changed;\n3. For projects in use but not organized yet, list them for me first and complete their documents with the wizard only after I agree; do not move, delete or edit the projects' own work files;\n4. Register every workflow's CEO in the CEO roster documentation/ROLES.md: run `agentj wizard register --dir . --json`, then check with `agentj wizard doctor --dir . --json`;\n5. For each company with only a CEO and no staff yet (its card says so), read its latest reports/, task.json and the roles in RUN.md, propose 3–7 staff roles (name, what each does, when to send it) and list them for me first; only after I agree, write them with `agentj wizard apply` to `<folder>/.claude/agents/<role>.md` (the Codex `.codex/agents/<role>.toml` is made with it), never over files I changed;\n6. Finally tell me what you registered, what you added, what is still missing, and which cards the phone's Workflows page will show.",
  "p276.reviewPrompt": "Please use the agentj-workflow-wizard skill (the Workflow Design Bible method) to review my organization. This is a review, not a redo:\n1. Look at the folders one level under the working root against the CEO roster documentation/ROLES.md and find new projects that are not registered;\n2. For organized ones, only review the entry file and the documentation/ boot documents; fill gaps with `agentj wizard apply`, never over files I changed;\n3. List new, unorganized projects for me first and complete them with the wizard only after I agree; do not move, delete or edit the projects' own work files;\n4. Run `agentj wizard register --dir . --json` to fill the roster, then check with `agentj wizard doctor --dir . --json`;\n5. For each company with only a CEO and no staff yet (its card says so), read its latest reports/, task.json and the roles in RUN.md, propose 3–7 staff roles (name, what each does, when to send it) and list them for me first; only after I agree, write them with `agentj wizard apply` to `<folder>/.claude/agents/<role>.md` (the Codex `.codex/agents/<role>.toml` is made with it), never over files I changed;\n6. Tell me only what this review found and fixed, what is still missing, and which cards the phone's Workflows page will show.",
